{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>When you go out</b> Why is the portion of the decapitated heifer written between two wars? War was placed before it — lest the enemy say: I killed him because it is a time of war, and the enemies will say: they killed him in battle. And war is written after it, to say: avenge the innocent blood by killing the murderer, and afterward go out to war and prevail. And they would not allow enemies to go out to war together, lest they kill each other in battle." "<b>that you do what is right</b> And adjacent to it: <b>when you go out to war</b> — none go out to war except the righteous." "<b>HaShem</b> And adjacent to it: <b>when you go out</b> ל.מ.לחמה — to say that HaShem goes out with you, as it says: \"and HaShem will go out and fight against the nations.\"" "<b>When you go out</b> Go out against them and do not let them come upon you, lest they destroy the land." "<b>your enemy</b> Defective (missing yod) — the verse speaks of a war of the individual." "<b>and its captivity</b> In gematria: ואם יהיו כנענים (\"and if they are Canaanites\") = שביו."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:10.529082411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}